## Hurricane Sandy and the Bridge Cafe (October 2012)

Alexis worked through this period at the historic Bridge Cafe (279

Water St, the city's oldest continuously operating tavern), a job that

had started while the couple still lived at Bedford Ave but continued

into the 90th Street year. Hurricane Sandy's October 2012 flooding of

the Seaport district closed the Bridge Cafe, ending Alexis's employment

there — a real economic shock to the household roughly six months

before the couple's return to Uniontown, and worth noting as landing

during this address's occupancy rather than the earlier Bedford Ave

years, where it is sometimes loosely attributed.

